Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:26:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Pages: /fun is the hashfun site of this machine,
 /fun/p2p/TICKER a line to its launches' nodes

On a node that is the site, /fun passes through to hashfun's pages on
FUN_WEB_PORT, as they are (bodies up to 1 MB), the header links to it
(fun: the coins these nodes mine) and the front has the site's two lines.
/fun/p2p/TICKER is a WebSocket carried to the site's own node of that launch
and to nothing else, whatever the request names: a few lines per address
and per launch, a silent line closed, a side that stops reading holding the
other back by one chunk. A node that is not a site has neither.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014XWxCQ3HRkxqr38zmdadwu
